Expected elements: MISSING — a timeline or scrubber expressing position within the trace

That absence is finding #1, it is P1, and my rating is 4. There is no track, elapsed run or playhead anywhere in the identity bar or in any pane; only the `128 / 1315` fraction. The loop strip in the Code pane scrubs one loop, not the trace.

On colour: this is not a dark theme inverted — the light surface is deliberate and the register still reads as a tool, not as marketing. The cyan position family is well chosen and is genuinely doing one job in the Code gutter and the Call Trace.

The problem is that two hue families each carry two meanings. Amber is both the `Partial` outcome badge and the changed-at-this-step marker, so an outcome badge and a mutated numeral are the same colour on one screen. Blue is the hyperlink role, the active phase chip and the non-interactive `Synthetic demo data` badge, which is outlined and tinted like a link and is not one. And the one surface where a position mark still exists — the loop tick strip — marks the current iteration in neutral grey, not in the position colour used two panes away.

Surface levels are thin: banner, identity bar and pane interiors are all the same white, separated only by hairlines.

Highest-priority fixes: (1) split the amber role — outcome badges off the changed-value family; (2) put the loop strip's current tick on the position colour.

Rating: 4/10

